From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Mar 2026 09:12:18 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS/ARM64 port of FEXCore for jailed iOS devices
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Port FEXCore to compile and run as a static library on iOS (arm64).
Key changes:

Build system:
- Skip Source/, Data/binfmts/, Data/AppConfig/ on Apple
- Disable jemalloc/rpmalloc, use system malloc
- Skip 64BitAllocator on Apple

Linux→Apple compatibility:
- prctl stubs, sigprocmask instead of SYS_rt_sigprocmask
- Spin-wait+usleep instead of futex (WritePriorityMutex, InterruptableConditionVariable)
- malloc_size instead of malloc_usable_size, posix_memalign instead of memalign
- sincos → sin+cos, fcopyfile instead of sendfile
- Relaxed InternalThreadState size assertions (Apple shared_mutex is larger)
- x18 excluded from register allocation (Apple platform TLS)

Dual-mapped JIT memory (W^X compliance):
- Buffer.h: WriteOffset/WritePtr for RX→RW translation
- JIT.cpp: SetWriteOffset(0) for TempCodeBuffer, restore for CodeBuffer
- Emitter.h: Forward label Bind() uses WritePtr for memory access
- Dispatcher.cpp: Split i-cache invalidation (data cache on RW, icache on RX)

Tested on iPhone 13 Pro (A15), iOS 26.3 — x86-64 exit(42) passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
